-- title:
--   Supersingular DVR over small constants with base-layer stalks
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` and, for a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $\kappa$ denotes `ResidueField A`.
--
--   Function fields involved. For a field $k$, `modularFunctionFieldC k M'` is the subfield of `LaurentSeries k` generated over $k$ by the two series `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k M'`. The field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` is the subfield of `LaurentSeries ℚ` generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the series `qExpand ℚ d jq` for the divisors $d$ of $M'$, and `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of `LaurentSeries ℚbar` generated by the coefficientwise images of that field. Finally `fieldBar q M'` is `xHFunctionFieldBar (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of `LaurentSeries ℚbar` generated by the coefficientwise images of `xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the subgroup of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$.
--
--   Data and hypotheses. Fixed are: a prime $q$ with $5 \le q$ (`hq`); a non-zero $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`); a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `hA : A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ which by `hW` consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' κ`, the places $w$ that are rational (the structure map $\kappa \to w$'s residue field is surjective), satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace κ M' w`, and have `w.evalAt (jGeomGen κ M') ∈ ssJSet q κ`; the inclusion `hle : modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`; a constant reduction $R_0$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` relative to $A$ with residue field `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`, that is, a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective homomorphism `R₀.residue` from it onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` with kernel the maximal ideal, restricting on constants to $A$ and inducing $A \to \kappa$ there, such that every non-zero function becomes integral with non-zero residue after multiplication by a constant, together with a map `R₀.placeMap` on places preserving degrees and carrying the divisor of any function of non-zero residue to the divisor of its residue; the hypothesis `hR₀`, which says that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and the Laurent series underlying its $R_0$-residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$; and a chosen element $s$ of $W$.
--
--   The small constants. $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lies in $A$ (`hπ`). Writing $A_0 =$ `A.comap (algebraMap k₀ ℚbar)` for $A \cap k_0$, the hypotheses are: $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), it is a henselian local ring (`hhens`), its residue field is algebraically closed (`hres`), and (`hκ`) every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element $c$ of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   Auxiliary constants. $\ell$ is a prime with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (`hζ₀`); $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lies in $A$ (`hϖtA`) and satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   The base layer of constants. $K_b$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_b = \bot$ (`hKb`, so $K_b = k_0$), $A_b$ is a valuation subring of $K_b$ whose elements are exactly those lying in $A$ (`hAb`), and $\varpi_b \neq 0$ (`hϖb0`) generates the maximal ideal of $A_b$ (`hϖb`).
--
--   Conclusion. Regard `fieldBar q M'` as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`. Then there exist an intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ and a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ such that the following nine assertions hold.
--
--   (1) The join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the range of $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'` is the whole field.
--
--   (2) For $x \in k_0$: $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (3) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   (4) The image of $\pi_0$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (5) There is $t \in W_0$ with the following property: for every polynomial $p \in k_0[X]$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$, then every coefficient of $p$ has its image in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (6) For every Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb Q$ lying in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, whose image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers`, such that for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ the inequality $0 \le \operatorname{ord}_P$ of the image of `jq` implies $0 \le \operatorname{ord}_P$ of the image of $g$, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$: the image of $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` under `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` lies in $F_0$, the resulting element of $F_0$ lies in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals `s.evalAt` of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of that element and the image of $c$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (7) For every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (the primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma \in SL(2,\mathbb Z)$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$, the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ maps $F_0$ into itself, and for $f \in F_0$ with image again in $F_0$ one has $f \in W_0$ if and only if its image lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (8) For every intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ finite over $k_0$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to$ `fieldBar q M'` with all $a_i$ in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$: if $c$ is linearly independent over $K'$ and $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$, then $a_i = 0$ for all $i$.
--
--   (9) For every field $FSS$ that is an algebra over $\kappa$ and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ on `fieldBar q M'` with residue field $FSS$ (a valuation subring `R.integers` with a surjective residue homomorphism onto $FSS$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, restricting to $A$ on constants and inducing $A \to \kappa$, with the scaling property above) such that for $f \in F_0$ one has $f \in$ `R.integers` if and only if $f \in W_0$, the following two statements hold.
--
--   (9a) For every algebra structure of `GaloisField q 2` on $\kappa$, every proof that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain and every $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of `rootsOfUnity (q + 1) (GaloisField q 2)` and an isomorphism $e$ of $\kappa$-algebras from $FSS$ onto [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32), the subfield of the Drinfeld function field `drinfeldFunctionField q κ` fixed by the subgroup generated by the actions of the elements $(1,\zeta')$ with $\zeta' \in C_s$, such that: the cardinality of $C_s$ is $2\,$`placeWidthChar q M' s`, where `placeWidthChar q M' s` is `jWidthChar q (s.evalAt (jGeomGen κ M'))` divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s`; and for every $\gamma \in SL(2,\mathbb Z)$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$, given that `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` preserves `R.integers` and that $(\mathrm{redQ}_q\gamma, 1)$ lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of $(\gamma',\zeta') \mapsto \det(\gamma')\zeta'^{\,q+1}$ on $GL_2(\mathbb Z/q) \times \mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$), for every $x \in FSS$ the image of $e(R.\mathrm{resAut}(\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1})\,x)$ in the Drinfeld function field equals [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) at $(\mathrm{redQ}_q\gamma,1)$ applied to the image of $e(x)$.
--
--   (9b) There exist a finite set $N$ of places of $FSS$ over $\kappa$, an assignment $Q \mapsto S_Q$ of subrings of `fieldBar q M'`, ring homomorphisms $\varphi_Q : A_b[X] \to S_Q$ and $\chi_Q : S_Q \to \kappa$, and an assignment $Q \mapsto D_Q$ of sets of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, such that $N$ has exactly $q+1$ elements and, for every place $Q \notin N$: the image in `fieldBar q M'` of every $a \in A_b$ lies in $S_Q$; $\varphi_Q(C\,a)$ equals that image for every $a \in A_b$; $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q(C\,a))$ is the residue in $\kappa$ of $a$, for every $a \in A_b$; $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q(X)) = 0$; $S_Q$ carries a local ring structure for which the kernel of $\chi_Q$ is the maximal ideal; $S_Q$ is contained in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_b$, and every element $f$ of that join satisfies $f\,h = g$ for some $g, h \in S_Q$ with $h \ne 0$; $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type; every element of $S_Q$ lies in `R.integers`, and for $f \in S_Q$ its image lies in the maximal ideal of `R.integers` if and only if $\varphi_Q(C\,\varpi_b)$ divides $f$ in $S_Q$; for every $f \in S_Q$ the $R$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and its residue in the residue field of $Q$ is the image of $\chi_Q(f)$ under $\kappa \to$ `Q.ResidueField`; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_Q(X)$ has $Q$-order equal to $1$; and a place $P$ belongs to $D_Q$ precisely when $P$ is rational, every $f \in S_Q$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with `P.evalAt f` in $A$, and for every $f \in S_Q$ the valuation of `P.evalAt f` in $A$ is $< 1$ if and only if $\chi_Q(f) = 0$.
--
--   In addition: if $Q, Q' \notin N$ and some place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` lies in both $D_Q$ and $D_{Q'}$, then $Q = Q'$; for $Q \notin N$ and $P \in D_Q$ the order at $P$ of the image of `jq` in `fieldBar q M'` is $\ge 0$; and for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of automorphisms of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta$ in `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, if $\tau$ preserves `R.integers` then for every place $Q$ of $FSS$ one has $R.\mathrm{resAut}(\tau) \cdot Q \in N$ if and only if $Q \in N$, and if $Q \notin N$ then $\{P : \tau^{-1}\cdot P \in D_Q\} = D_{R.\mathrm{resAut}(\tau)\cdot Q}$.
--
--   This is the base-layer case $K_b = k_0$ of the construction, over a field of small constants, of a discrete valuation ring on the full-level modular function field of level $q^2M'$ at a supersingular point, together with the data describing the stalks at the smooth points of the corresponding component of the special fibre, which is identified with a quotient of the Drinfeld curve. It is the constructor's core of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointStalks`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointStalks), which propagates the same package through the finite layers of constants; the proof assembles [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_affineChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_affineChart), [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_existDL_of_affineChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_existDL_of_affineChart) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_ends_baseSmoothPointStalks_of_affineChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_ends_baseSmoothPointStalks_of_affineChart).
